sanjay: Heads-up — Vantage Corp wants to prove we can replace CompetitorX as a near drop-in for their customer-facing text generation. They flagged three must-haves: identical request/response shapes for our common endpoints, streaming parity, and a security questionnaire answered before their legal/infosec review. Need a quick plan and who owns what.
marie-se: I can run the POC plan. Quick Qs: which endpoints they call most? chat vs completions vs embeddings? any custom headers or param names they rely on?
tom-eng: They mostly use the /v1/complete-style endpoint and have a tiny shim that sets `model=comp-x`, `max_tokens` and `stop` as arrays. Biggest friction is that CompetitorX returns `choices[]` with `delta` chunks for streaming; our streaming uses event-stream with `data: {
